(5541665, 799093, 69008, '<td valign="top">The straight line of the top of a wall going right through the top of the biker''s head probably dinged this a lot in voting.  Had he been a little lower or you a little higher, you could have cropped the bright area out, and it would be much more voter friendly. It''s still a good, well exposed  pan shot. Focus and following were spot on.</td>', 'The straight line of the top of a wall going right through the top of the biker''s head probably dinged this a lot in voting.  Had he been a little lower or you a little higher, you could have cropped the bright area out, and it would be much more voter friendly. It''s still a good, well exposed  pan shot. Focus and following were spot on.', '2009-06-24 02:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541668, 799495, 51638, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this didn''t do better. It''s a classic bike magazine type image.</td>', 'I''m surprised this didn''t do better. It''s a classic bike magazine type image.', '2009-06-24 02:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541679, 798383, 51638, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bspurgeon:</b></div><hr/><i> Yeah, I wondered if this would finish below mine. Personally, I don''t see how you can get this shot without panning. Unless it''s fake, you must pan, and do it well to get this capture. Obviously the voters wanted streaking...meh! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry, but with a shutter speed of 1/1000 I think it''s perfectly plausible for this to have been captured without panning.</td>', 'Originally posted by bspurgeon: Yeah, I wondered if this would finish below mine. Personally, I don''t see how you can get this shot without panning. Unless it''s fake, you must pan, and do it well to get this capture. Obviously the voters wanted streaking...meh!   Sorry, but with a shutter speed of 1/1000 I think it''s perfectly plausible for this to have been captured without panning.', '2009-06-24 02:15:11.000000', NULL, 0),
