(5541733, 799093, 39427, '<td valign="top">i actually think its a cool, well composed shot, not worthy of a 5.0, but I can see why it didn''t ''kill''... for one, I think the cool colors of the majority of the image (in the shade) contrast too much with the warm colors of the direct sunlight in the background... and aside from the the warmth/coolness factor, the brightness is also slightly unsettling.  But the biggest thing i would say is the lack of ''critical'' focus on the subject... motion panning is an all or nothing gig, if you''re not 100% in focus on PART of the image, people will fault you for it... here, the head &amp; face are a bit shaky and that will hurt you.  Don''t think it deserved as low as it did but those are my 2 cents</td>', 'i actually think its a cool, well composed shot, not worthy of a 5.0, but I can see why it didn''t ''kill''... for one, I think the cool colors of the majority of the image (in the shade) contrast too much with the warm colors of the direct sunlight in the background... and aside from the the warmth/coolness factor, the brightness is also slightly unsettling.  But the biggest thing i would say is the lack of ''critical'' focus on the subject... motion panning is an all or nothing gig, if you''re not 100% in focus on PART of the image, people will fault you for it... here, the head & face are a bit shaky and that will hurt you.  Don''t think it deserved as low as it did but those are my 2 cents', '2009-06-24 03:05:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541735, 799779, 41357, '<td valign="top">only one place short from the brown ribbon<br/>u failed again!<br/>nice pic</td>', 'only one place short from the brown ribbonu failed again!nice pic', '2009-06-24 03:06:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541744, 799093, 53964, '<td valign="top">For me it''s how the lightest part of the biker is his butt, so my eye keeps being drawn back there instead of to his face and arms, where more of the interest should be :)<br/> <br/>I do love the grafittied wall behind him, and I like (tho'' some won''t) the fact that the bike is blurred while he isn''t. That said, he''s sharp in comparison but not DPC tack-sharp.</td>', 'For me it''s how the lightest part of the biker is his butt, so my eye keeps being drawn back there instead of to his face and arms, where more of the interest should be :) I do love the grafittied wall behind him, and I like (tho'' some won''t) the fact that the bike is blurred while he isn''t. That said, he''s sharp in comparison but not DPC tack-sharp.', '2009-06-24 03:16:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541767, 798383, 106109, '<td valign="top">I would like to suggest a personal challenge to all of you who say that this photo could be taken without panning.<br/> <br/>Attach a 300mm lens, point it up in the sky anywhere, then wait for a Purple Martin to fly through your FOV and press the shutter button. I would <b>LOVE</b> to see your results!!!!</td>', 'I would like to suggest a personal challenge to all of you who say that this photo could be taken without panning. Attach a 300mm lens, point it up in the sky anywhere, then wait for a Purple Martin to fly through your FOV and press the shutter button. I would LOVE to see your results!!!!', '2009-06-24 03:35:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541769, 798247, 74677, '<td valign="top">Thanks for everyone, I glad to get my firs ribbon :)<br/>This is the my Beagle his name Ramzis.</td>', 'Thanks for everyone, I glad to get my firs ribbon :)This is the my Beagle his name Ramzis.', '2009-06-24 03:38:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541792, 799729, 39427, '<td valign="top">a great <i>moment</i> you''ve captured but I would say 1) too pixelated, 2) barely any pan and 3) too zoomed out for an action shot of this sort... and I know its a pain I can only go to 200mm myself!  I think if this were cropped into just the bird and the reflection it would be a standout shot, even if the bird is facing outwards</td>', 'a great moment you''ve captured but I would say 1) too pixelated, 2) barely any pan and 3) too zoomed out for an action shot of this sort... and I know its a pain I can only go to 200mm myself!  I think if this were cropped into just the bird and the reflection it would be a standout shot, even if the bird is facing outwards', '2009-06-24 03:50:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5541799, 800028, 6783, '<td valign="top">Hi. Congrats for your placement.<br/>I have a technical  question about the photo, if you don''t mind:<br/>With the settings as stated, how did you compensate for the overexposure? Did you used any nd filter? 1/20 of a second at f/5.0 is a lot of light... While shooting my attempts with similar settings I was forced to use a 6x nd filter and it was still too much exposed...</td>', 'Hi. Congrats for your placement.I have a technical  question about the photo, if you don''t mind:With the settings as stated, how did you compensate for the overexposure? Did you used any nd filter? 1/20 of a second at f/5.0 is a lot of light... While shooting my attempts with similar settings I was forced to use a 6x nd filter and it was still too much exposed...', '2009-06-24 03:57:43.000000', NULL, 0),
