(5542463, 799793, 83845, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lutchenko:</b></div><hr/><i> I have a sneaking suspicion that what we may be looking at here is a stationary bubble and a moving brick rather then motion panning </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I somehow doubt that, since it''s an entire wall of bricks! hahaha </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL, thanks <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a>, it is also impossible to make a bubble stand still... that I am aware of anyway.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Originally posted by Lutchenko: I have a sneaking suspicion that what we may be looking at here is a stationary bubble and a moving brick rather then motion panning  I somehow doubt that, since it''s an entire wall of bricks! hahaha   LOL, thanks  posthumous, it is also impossible to make a bubble stand still... that I am aware of anyway.', '2009-06-24 14:02:32.000000', NULL, 0),
